p(28,2,"As soon as my knees were sufficiently healed I was turned",
 "Black Beauty is left alone in a meadow and feels lonely. Then Ginger is brought in; she has been ruined by hard riding.",
 "As soon as my knees were well enough, I was put in a small meadow for a month or two. No other animal was there, and although I enjoyed the freedom and the sweet grass, I had lived with other horses for so long that I felt very lonely. Ginger and I had become close friends, and now I missed her very much. I often neighed when I heard horses’ feet passing in the road, but I seldom got an answer. Then one morning the gate was opened, and who should come in but dear old Ginger! The man took off her halter and left her there. I trotted up to her with a happy whinny. We were both glad to meet, but I soon found that she was not brought to be with me for our pleasure. Her story would be too long to tell, but the end of it was that hard riding had ruined her, and she was now sent away to see what rest would do.",
 ["sufficiently","society","neighed","halter","joyful","whinny","ruined","turned off"])
s(28,"Lord George was young and would take no warning",
 "Lord George was young and did not listen to any warning.",
 "'would take no warning' uses 'would' for something that was always true of him in the past; it means 'was not willing to'.") if False else None
s(28,"The mare shall have a twelvemonth’s run, and we shall see",
 "The mare will have a year in the field, and we will see how good that is for her.",
 "'shall' with 'she' or 'we' here shows the earl's decision, not just the future; 'twelvemonth’s run' is a year of free time in a field.")
