p(29,7,"Besides, these drivers are often careless altogether",
 "A careless driver lets a stone get into the horse's foot. He laughs and jokes with the lady and children, and does not look at the road or his horse.",
 "These drivers are also often careless altogether, and pay attention to anything else more than their horses. One day I went out in the phaeton with one of them. He had a lady and two children behind. He moved the reins about loosely as we started, and gave me several cuts with the whip for no reason, although I had already started well. There had been a lot of road-mending, and even where the stones were not freshly laid there were many loose ones about. My driver was laughing and joking with the lady and the children and talking about the country on the right and the left. But he never thought it worth the trouble to watch his horse or to drive on the smoothest parts of the road. So it easily happened that I got a stone in one of my front feet.",
 ["flopped","unmeaning","phaeton","fore"])
s(29,"Now, if Mr. Gordon or John, or in fact any good driver, had been there",
 "","") if False else None
s(29,"a practiced hand would have felt by the rein that there was something",
 "A driver who knew his job would have felt through the rein that something was wrong with the horse's step.",
 "'would have felt' is the third conditional result: it says what a good driver would have done, but this driver did not.")
